        <p id="shouldWrapAtHigherLevel-precedence">
          The following table shows the operator precedence hierarchy used when
          <code>shouldWrapAtHigherLevel</code> is enabled, ordered from highest
          precedence (tighter binding, lower syntactical level) to lowest precedence
          (looser binding, higher syntactical level). Wrapping at a higher syntactical level
          (lower precedence) is preferred over wrapping at a lower syntactical level:
        </p>
        <div class="wrapper">
          <table>
            <tr>
              <th>Precedence Level</th>
              <th>Operators</th>
              <th>TokenTypes</th>
              <th>Description</th>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>1</td>
              <td><code>::</code></td>
              <td><code>METHOD_REF</code></td>
              <td>Method reference</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>2</td>
              <td><code>*</code>, <code>/</code>, <code>%</code></td>
              <td><code>STAR</code>, <code>DIV</code>, <code>MOD</code></td>
              <td>Multiplicative</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>3</td>
              <td><code>+</code>, <code>-</code></td>
              <td><code>PLUS</code>, <code>MINUS</code></td>
              <td>Additive</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>4</td>
              <td><code>&lt;&lt;</code>, <code>&gt;&gt;</code>, <code>&gt;&gt;&gt;</code></td>
              <td><code>SL</code>, <code>SR</code>, <code>BSR</code></td>
              <td>Shift</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>5</td>
              <td><code>&lt;</code>, <code>&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;=</code>, <code>&gt;=</code>, <code>instanceof</code></td>
              <td><code>LT</code>, <code>GT</code>, <code>LE</code>, <code>GE</code>, <code>LITERAL_INSTANCEOF</code></td>
              <td>Relational</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>6</td>
              <td><code>==</code>, <code>!=</code></td>
              <td><code>EQUAL</code>, <code>NOT_EQUAL</code></td>
              <td>Equality</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>7</td>
              <td><code>&amp;</code></td>
              <td><code>BAND</code></td>
              <td>Bitwise AND</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>8</td>
              <td><code>^</code></td>
              <td><code>BXOR</code></td>
              <td>Bitwise XOR</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>9</td>
              <td><code>|</code></td>
              <td><code>BOR</code></td>
              <td>Bitwise OR</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>10</td>
              <td><code>&amp;&amp;</code></td>
              <td><code>LAND</code></td>
              <td>Logical AND</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>11</td>
              <td><code>||</code></td>
              <td><code>LOR</code></td>
              <td>Logical OR</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>12</td>
              <td><code>? :</code></td>
              <td><code>QUESTION</code>, <code>COLON</code></td>
              <td>Ternary / conditional</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>13</td>
              <td><code>=</code>, <code>+=</code>, <code>-=</code>, <code>*=</code>, etc.</td>
              <td><code>ASSIGN</code>, <code>PLUS_ASSIGN</code>, etc.</td>
              <td>Assignment</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>14</td>
              <td><code>-&gt;</code></td>
              <td><code>LAMBDA</code></td>
              <td>Lambda expression</td>
            </tr>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p id="Example4-config">
          To configure the check for higher level operator wrapping:
        </p>
        <div class="wrapper"><pre class="prettyprint"><code class="language-xml">
&lt;module name="Checker"&gt;
  &lt;module name="TreeWalker"&gt;
    &lt;module name="OperatorWrap"&gt;
      &lt;property name="shouldWrapAtHigherLevel" value="true"/&gt;
    &lt;/module&gt;
  &lt;/module&gt;
&lt;/module&gt;
</code></pre></div>
        <p id="Example4-code">
         Example:
        </p>
        <div class="wrapper"><pre class="prettyprint"><code class="language-java">
class Example4 {
  void example() {
    String s = "Hello" +
      "World"; // violation above ''\+' should be on a new line'

    if (10 ==
            20) { // violation above ''==' should be on a new line'
    }

    int c = 10 /
            5; // violation above ''/' should be on a new line'

    int b
            = 10;
    int e =
            10;
    b
            += 10;
    b +=
            10;
    c
            *= 10;
    c
            -= 5;
    c -=
            5;
    c
            /= 2;
    c
            %= 1;
    c
            &gt;&gt;= 1;
    c
        &gt;&gt;&gt;= 1;
    c
            &amp;=1 ;
    c
            &lt;&lt;= 1;

    int a = 1;
    int b1 = 2;
    int c1 = 3;
    int x4 = a / (b1
            - c1); // violation above ''/' should be on a new line'
  }
}
</code></pre></div>
